<title>BAHRAIN: Bahrain's GIB appoints new general manager.</title>
<headline>Bahrain's GIB appoints new general manager.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gulf International Bank (GIB) said on Sunday it had appointed Abdullah al-Quwaiz, Saudi Arabia's deputy finance minister for economic affairs, as its new general manager.</p>
<p>A bank statement said Quwaiz replaces Ghazi Abdul-Jawad, who resigned recently to become from February 1 the new president and chief executive of the Arab Banking Corporation ABC, replacing Ahmed Abdullatif.</p>
<p>GIB is wholly owned by Kuwait-based Gulf Investment Corp, in turn owned by the Gulf Cooperation Council which groups Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, Bahrain, Qatar, Oman and the United Arab Emirates.</p>
